  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{TeO}_2$ is oxidizing in nature because it can be reduced from +4 oxidation state to lower oxidation state.<br />$\\mathrm{TeH}_2$ due to less bond dissociation energy easily breaks and hence acidic in nature.",
    "image": null
  },
